    <string-array name="tip_neutral">
        <item>Write down expenses right away — in the evening half of them are forgotten.</item>
        <item>Small daily purchases add up: coffee every day is a whole trip a year.</item>
        <item>Set limits on 2–3 main categories — that’s enough to see the picture.</item>
        <item>Before a big purchase, wait 48 hours. If you still want it — buy it.</item>
        <item>Put aside part of your income on payday, not at the end of the month.</item>
        <item>Check subscriptions: some of them you probably don’t use.</item>
        <item>A goal with a deadline is reached faster than “someday”.</item>
        <item>Compare this month with last one in Analytics — it’s very motivating.</item>
        <item>Shopping lists save up to 20% at the supermarket.</item>
        <item>A streak of records is a habit. Don’t break it!</item>
    </string-array>
